<title>USA: GM May U.S. vehicle sales fall 8.1 pct.</title>
<headline>GM May U.S. vehicle sales fall 8.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp</p>
<p>			May 1-31, 1997     May 1-31, 1996 *Pct Chng</p>
<p> Total Car		250,887	   300,780	    -16.6</p>
<p> Total Truck	    199,943	   189,742	     +5.4</p>
<p> Total Vehicle	  450,830	   490,522	     -8.1</p>
<p>		  Jan 1-May 31, 1997 Jan 1-May 31, 1996 *Pct Chng</p>
<p> Total Car	    1,126,402	 1,232,613	     -7.9</p>
<p> Total Truck	    865,523	   851,296	     +2.5</p>
<p> Total Vehicle	1,991,925	 2,083,909	     -3.7</p>
<p>* Pct change based on daily selling rate. Sale days 26 in latest month vs 26, 128 for year to date vs 129 in year ago.</p>
<p>NOTE: Total GM car sales include U.S. sales figures from Saab Automobile AB, which is 50 percent owned by GM and 50 percent owned by Sweden's AB Investor.</p>
</text>
